    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def classify_intent(query):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    query_lower = query.lower()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    intent_keywords = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"code\": [\"code\", \"function\", \"bug\", \"error\", \"file\", \"implement\", \"refactor\", \"debug\", \"test\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"calendar\": [\"meeting\", \"schedule\", \"calendar\", \"appointment\", \"event\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"email\": [\"email\", \"mail\", \"send\", \"inbox\", \"message\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"research\": [\"search\", \"find\", \"what is\", \"how does\", \"explain\", \"look up\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"data\": [\"data\", \"query\", \"database\", \"chart\", \"graph\", \"analytics\", \"sql\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scores = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for intent, keywords in intent_keywords.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        score = sum(1 for kw in keywords if kw in query_lower)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if score > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            scores[intent] = score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not scores:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [\"code\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    max_score = max(scores.values())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [intent for intent, score in scores.items() if score >= max_score * 0.5]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def select_tools(query, token_budget=2000):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    intents = classify_intent(query)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    relevant = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_tokens = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for name, tool in TOOL_REGISTRY.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if any(cat in intents for cat in tool[\"categories\"]):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if total_tokens + tool[\"tokens\"] <= token_budget:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                relevant[name] = tool"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                total_tokens += tool[\"tokens\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return relevant, total_tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Full Context Assembly Pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Wire everything together. Given a query, dynamically assemble the optimal context."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class ContextEngine:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, max_tokens=128000, generation_reserve=4000):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.budget = ContextBudget(max_tokens, generation_reserve)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conversation = ConversationManager(max_history_tokens=5000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.system_prompt = ("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"You are a helpful AI assistant. You have access to tools for \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"code editing, file management, web search, and data analysis. \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"Use the appropriate tools for each task. Be concise and accurate.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.knowledge_base = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"Python 3.12 introduced type parameter syntax for generic classes using bracket notation.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"The project uses PostgreSQL 16 with pgvector for embedding storage.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"Authentication is handled by Supabase Auth with JWT tokens.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"The frontend is built with Next.js 15 using the App Router.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"API rate limits are set to 100 requests per minute per user.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"The deployment pipeline uses GitHub Actions with Docker multi-stage builds.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"Test coverage must be above 80% for all new modules.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"The codebase follows the repository pattern for data access.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def assemble(self, query):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.budget = ContextBudget(self.budget.max_tokens, self.budget.generation_reserve)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        system_content, _ = self.budget.allocate(\"system_prompt\", self.system_prompt, max_tokens=1000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tools, tool_tokens = select_tools(query, token_budget=2000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tool_text = json.dumps(list(tools.keys()))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tool_content, _ = self.budget.allocate(\"tools\", tool_text, max_tokens=2000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        relevance = score_relevance(query, self.knowledge_base)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        threshold = 0.1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        relevant_docs = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            doc for doc, score in zip(self.knowledge_base, relevance)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if score >= threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if relevant_docs:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            doc_scores = [s for s in relevance if s >= threshold]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            reordered = reorder_lost_in_middle(relevant_docs, doc_scores)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            doc_text = \"\\n\".join(reordered)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            doc_content, _ = self.budget.allocate(\"retrieved_context\", doc_text, max_tokens=3000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        history_text = self.conversation.get_context()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if history_text.strip():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            history_content, _ = self.budget.allocate(\"conversation_history\", history_text, max_tokens=5000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        query_content, _ = self.budget.allocate(\"user_query\", query, max_tokens=500)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.budget"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def chat(self, query):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conversation.add_turn(\"user\", query)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        budget = self.assemble(query)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        response = f\"[Response to: {query[:50]}...]\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.conversation.add_turn(\"assistant\", response)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return budget"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def run_demo():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"=\" * 60)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"  Context Engineering Pipeline Demo\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"=\" * 60)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    engine = ContextEngine(max_tokens=128000, generation_reserve=4000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"\\n--- Query 1: Code task ---\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    budget = engine.chat(\"Fix the bug in the authentication module where JWT tokens expire too early\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(budget.report())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"\\n--- Query 2: Research task ---\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    budget = engine.chat(\"What is the best approach for implementing vector search in PostgreSQL?\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(budget.report())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"\\n--- Query 3: After conversation history builds up ---\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(8):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        engine.conversation.add_turn(\"user\", f\"Follow-up question number {i+1} about the implementation details of the system\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        engine.conversation.add_turn(\"assistant\", f\"Here is the response to follow-up {i+1} with technical details about the architecture\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    budget = engine.chat(\"Now implement the changes we discussed\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(budget.report())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"\\n--- Tool Selection Examples ---\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    test_queries = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"Fix the bug in auth.py\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"Schedule a meeting with the team for Tuesday\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"Show me the database query performance stats\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"Search for best practices on error handling\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for q in test_queries:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tools, tokens = select_tools(q)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        intents = classify_intent(q)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"\\n  Query: {q}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"  Intents: {intents}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"  Tools: {list(tools.keys())} ({tokens} tokens)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"\\n--- Lost-in-the-Middle Reordering ---\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    docs = [\"Doc A (most relevant)\", \"Doc B (somewhat relevant)\", \"Doc C (least relevant)\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            \"Doc D (relevant)\", \"Doc E (moderately relevant)\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scores = [0.95, 0.60, 0.20, 0.80, 0.50]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    reordered = reorder_lost_in_middle(docs, scores)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  Original order: {docs}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  Scores:         {scores}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  Reordered:      {reordered}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"  (Most relevant at start and end, least relevant in middle)\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a \"token waste detector\" to the ContextBudget class. It should flag components using more than 30% of the budget and suggest compression strategies specific to each component type (summarize history, prune tools, re-rank documents).\n\n2. Implement semantic deduplication for retrieved context. If two retrieved documents are more than 80% similar (by word overlap or cosine similarity of their embeddings), keep only the higher-scored one. Measure how much token budget this recovers.\n\n3. Build a \"context replay\" tool. Given a conversation transcript, replay it through the ContextEngine and visualize how the budget allocation changes turn by turn. Plot token usage per component over time. Identify the turn where context starts getting compressed.\n\n4. Implement a priority-based tool selector. Instead of binary include/exclude, assign each tool a relevance score to the current query. Include tools in descending relevance order until the tool budget is exhausted. Compare task performance with 5, 10, 20, and 50 tools included.\n\n5. Build a multi-strategy context compressor. Implement three compression strategies (truncation, summarization, extraction of key sentences) and benchmark them on a set of 20 documents. Measure the tradeoff between compression ratio and information retention (does the compressed version still contain the answer to the query?)."
      ]
